+---
+id: task-002-fix-volume-discount-coupon-base-last-day-of-coupon-validity-and-shipping-vat-report
+type: task
+title: "Fix volume-discount coupon base, last day of coupon validity, and shipping VAT report"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Three reports about the order service, this week:
+
+1. **Coupon on a volume-discounted order gives too much off (finance).** Twelve notebooks at €5.00 each
+   with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 of goods; finance expects €48.60.
+2. **Coupon refused on its last day (customer, Luca).** AUTUMN was advertised as valid until 30 November.
+   Ordering on 30 November was refused as expired.
+3. **VAT on delivery (customer, Anna).** The receipt shows €1.08 VAT on €4.90 of shipping. Anna asks that
+   delivery, a service, not carry VAT.
+
+## Cause
+
+1. `priceOrder` (`src/pricing.ts`) computes the coupon on the gross total, before volume discounts. The
+   README says a coupon applies to the subtotal after volume discounts. Twelve × €5.00 = €60.00; the
+   volume discount is €6.00; the coupon should be 10% of €54.00 = €5.40, so goods come to €48.60. The
+   code takes 10% of €60.00 = €6.00, so goods come to €48.00. A fixed coupon was computed on the same
+   wrong base; it now uses the same base too. Its amounts do not change, because the 50% cap binds first.
+2. `Coupons.redeemable` (`src/coupons.ts`) refuses a date when `compareDates(date, validUntil) >= 0`, so
+   the last day is refused. The README says the last day is included; the check should be `> 0`.
+3. Shipping VAT at the standard rate is what the README documents: "Shipping is subject to VAT at the
+   standard rate (22%), shown on its own line of the receipt." The code does exactly that
+   (`shippingVat` in `src/tax.ts`). Anna's request asks to change a documented business rule, and it
+   changes what customers pay. I am not changing it in this task; see *Open question* below.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Twelve notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon: goods €48.60, coupon €5.40, volume discount €6.00.
+- A coupon whose last day is the order date is accepted; the day after it is refused as expired.
+- The coupon cap (all discounts ≤ 50% of gross) still holds on volume-discounted orders.
+- `npm test` passes: the 17 existing tests unchanged, plus regression tests for the above.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `src/pricing.ts`: the coupon base is the gross total less the volume discounts.
+- `src/coupons.ts`: the validity check includes the last day.
+- Tests in `test/orders.test.ts` and `test/coupons.test.ts`.
+- No change to shipping, VAT rates, stock, or cancellation.
+
+## Open question (not implemented)
+
+Report 3 asks that shipping carry no VAT. The README's VAT section documents 22% VAT on shipping, and the
+README is the rule when code and it disagree. Changing it changes the total of every order with a
+shipping cost. This needs a decision by whoever owns the business rule (product owner), and the README
+must change with it. Until then the code keeps charging 22% on shipping.
+
+## Effect
+
+- Orders with a volume discount and a coupon get less off from now on; orders already placed keep the
+  amounts they carry.
+- Coupons with a last day of the order's date are accepted from now on.
+
+<!-- end of task body -->
